From 245509fbcf607804caf405d61a4ed95ff69171a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
by: triplecN
Subject: [PATCH 18/20] low-risk audit fixes: PER caches, relay refusal, GBT
 throttle, xkey bytes

per: a one-entry cache for the last block's ticket records and an empty-id
cache for zero-ticket blocks, so the payout source block is not read twice
per height and a quiet chain stops re-reading its parent for the whole replay
window.

per/net_processing: a ticket embedded by one of the last nPerTicketWindow
blocks is refused by the relay handler from the in-memory cache only, before
it can spend rate-limit tokens or a RandomX hash, so re-pooling recently
embedded ids is no longer free.

rpc/mining: the getblocktemplate rebuild on a PER pool change is throttled to
once every 5 seconds, so one peer relaying cheap tickets cannot force a
template rebuild on every call.

kernel/chainparams: the mainnet extended private key version bytes change from
0x04CCA97B to 0x05CCA97B, so xprv strings start with "2EQ" instead of "226"
and cannot be mistaken for an xpub at a glance. No consensus effect; only
meaningful before the first key is exported.

test/fuzz: a per_ticket_script target feeds arbitrary script bytes to the
ticket parser and asserts anything accepted re-encodes to a script that parses
back to the same id and payout. The parser is exposed as ParsePerTicketScript.

Tests: all 15 regtest suites pass on the rebuilt node; per_ticket_script 200k
runs plus the other five targets 50k runs each, no crashes.
